 ## [Unreleased]

+### Changed
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool `input` against the tool's declared JSON Schema
+  `inputSchema` before calling the executor (`required`, declared property types, and `enum`,
+  with extra properties passed through unchanged and no type coercion or default injection).
+  Static schemas are compiled once at `register` time so an invalid schema throws immediately
+  naming the tool; function-valued tool definitions compile and cache validators per schema
+  object. When input fails validation, `execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing
+  field paths and constraints — never echoing or logging offending values — instead of invoking
+  the executor or throwing, so the model can correct the call on the next tool round. Tools
+  that previously relied on receiving malformed input inside their executor to format custom
+  errors will no longer be called when `inputSchema` rejects the payload.
+
 ## [0.3.0] - 2026-09-17

